WEBVTT

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.200
The story until now.

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:12.820
Grumbling about, but not refusing John Matzo's request, Nozomu takes the stage.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.560
Forced to be a boy soprano, he abuses his vocal cords, but exits after two minutes of booing.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:18.980
At the backup chanson the next week,

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:21.820
he makes a mess of the recital and runs to the Piano Forest in despair, only to find the Comics Forest instead.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:26.570
A numbered ticket was forced upon him, and the moment he joined the autograph line, the man in front of him struck up a conversation.

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:35.590
The man gasped “In France, <i>manga</i> is called the ninth art”, and other such otanationalism that make up the current fad, leaving Nozomu exhausted.

00:00:35.590 --> 00:00:38.160
As the conversation turned to Grendizer's TV ratings,

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:44.390
his number was called and he approached the podium, only to see the artist Shiina going by the alias “Maple Pinpin”.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:47.930
“What're you up to?” “Well, a lot's happened.” They said to one another,

00:00:47.930 --> 00:00:52.000
then began discussing the dark clock tower he had made of rejected manuscripts and raw meat to warn when deadlines approached.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:57.830
At that moment, a far-off, otherworldly bell rang out. “Run away! The green one's coming!”

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:36.000
Speaking as a teacher, I wonder whether high school is necessary.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:44.540
As an emergency measure, perhaps I shouldn't attend school.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:44.710
Modern anime

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:44.880
is missing something.

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:45.040
That something is

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:45.180
Rambararu

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:45.380
Meaning

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:45.650
Adult characters

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.500
Well, well. Nowadays...

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:55.250
One's capability for emergency measures is tested!

00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:56.620
Capability for emergency measures?

00:02:56.620 --> 00:02:59.260
Like how you always end up in a pinch.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:02.640
A scandal suddenly occurs, and you claim illness and go to the hospital!

00:03:02.990 --> 00:03:06.680
Or guests suddenly show up, and you make strange snacks out of fish sausage and eggs!

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.400
Or enemies suddenly attack, and you fight using hangers found at the scene!

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.140
The kind of capability for emergency measures used to make it through that kind of pinch!

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:16.210
It's impossible for modern man to live without it!

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.980
What's wrong with just solving the root of the problem!?

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:22.310
They're emergency measures, so it's fine just dealing with the emergency.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:27.220
However, your teacher knows quite well that his class is good at this!

00:03:31.090 --> 00:03:32.210
Just today...

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.110
It's my birthday!

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:37.280
Did you know?

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:38.600
No, it's the first I've heard of it.

00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:41.020
It's fine, you don't have to do anything.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.620
Come on, we've got to celebrate somehow.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.170
Hold on a minute.

00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:47.910
Here you go.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.860
What do I do? I didn't bring anything either!

00:03:57.850 --> 00:03:58.980
Here...

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:19.640
Congratulations!

00:04:20.780 --> 00:04:22.640
Thank you all.

00:04:31.350 --> 00:04:35.870
Presents put forth as emergency measures at school are rather miserable, aren't they?

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:42.150
What do I do? I don't have any presents she'd appreciate, like the others did.

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.830
The thought is enough.

00:04:42.830 --> 00:04:45.330
I've got it! I can sing!

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:47.610
I'll sing as your present!

00:05:10.520 --> 00:05:11.810
That's more than enough!

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.270
Just as I thought, this class is exceptionally talented at emergency measures.

00:05:17.270 --> 00:05:19.550
I didn't find them effective at all!

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:32.270
Somehow I'll make it through next week's 
pairing-specific event with this photocopied book!

00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.280
Nice emergency measures.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.130
Melancholy of Majiru

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:36.200
Extra!

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:39.710
Lately, there's been a lot of -tans.

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:42.940
Maybe anime companies will be next.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:45.730
Ooh, I'd like to be Kyoto then!

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:46.920
No, that's me.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:48.440
I was before any of you.

00:05:48.650 --> 00:05:51.130
Can't you put it politely!?

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:52.930
Teacher, say something!

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.800
Leave the Rising Sun characters to me!

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.730
My eyebrows failed.

00:06:00.730 --> 00:06:02.640
... Nice emergency measures.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.670
Nice emergency measures!

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:06.990
That doesn't count!

00:06:11.450 --> 00:06:13.240
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:06:13.240 --> 00:06:15.970
I'm sorry for distracting you all by getting wet!

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:20.830
I washed all your gym clothes.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:23.160
If you just put them on, they'll dry out fast.

00:06:23.160 --> 00:06:25.550
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:26.160
That really is a common emergency measure.

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:30.920
Just as I thought, my class is exceptionally talented at emergency measures.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:33.670
Mankind's wisdom lies in emergency measures!

00:06:33.940 --> 00:06:35.190
14 Looks pretty fun.

00:06:36.170 --> 00:06:39.410
This is an emergency measure for when your face shows how exhausted you are.

00:06:39.410 --> 00:06:42.700
Wow, Chiri, you look pretty tired.

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:46.420
I do, don't I?

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:47.040
Yeah.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:48.200
It's because you're worn out!

00:06:48.350 --> 00:06:51.220
I should give you a facial massage as an emergency measure.

00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.220
Lymph! Lymph!

00:06:53.390 --> 00:06:54.140
There you go!

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:55.490
What kind of trick is this!?

00:06:55.970 --> 00:06:59.230
Teacher, it looks like you're gradually loving women less and less.

00:07:00.630 --> 00:07:04.220
Now that I think about it, it seems like the school board is watching me today.

00:07:04.220 --> 00:07:06.640
So it's good that your face is back to normal.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:09.060
The school board is watching us?

00:07:09.060 --> 00:07:11.380
Oh no, now I've got to be proper and get all dolled up.

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:14.590
Wouldn't it be worse if you did?

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:15.280
What do I do? I don't have lipstick with me.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:17.980
The rules were pretty strict at my middle school,

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:19.950
so colored lipstick was forbidden.

00:07:20.390 --> 00:07:22.690
I nibbled my lips like this so they'd turn red.

00:07:22.690 --> 00:07:24.060
I see!

00:07:26.160 --> 00:07:27.390
You're biting too hard!

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:30.850
{ka}I thought it was cold!

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:32.460
The window's broken!

00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:33.680
Cold air is getting in!

00:07:34.170 --> 00:07:36.670
{fu}Let's put a poster over it as an emergency measure!

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:40.370
It's no good! No matter what, the wind blows in!

00:07:40.370 --> 00:07:41.640
It's cold!

00:07:41.920 --> 00:07:46.180
Don't people play <i>oshikura manju</i> as an emergency measure when it's cold?{http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oshikura_Manju}

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:51.120
Oshikura manju!

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.520
Don't cry, even when you're shoved!

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:55.520
Hold it, that hurts!

00:08:00.460 --> 00:08:03.010
A dying message written in blood.

00:08:03.010 --> 00:08:05.200
That's an emergency measure when there's nothing to write with, right?

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:07.690
Even if it didn't save his life.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:08.830
What do we do?

00:08:08.830 --> 00:08:10.440
The man from the school board is coming!

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:14.290
At times like these, there's only one emergency measure.

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:15.870
Hide him under the floor.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:18.820
Won't they think it's strange that Teacher isn't here?

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:22.610
It's fine. There's a good emergency measure for that.

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:25.620
I see.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:33.090
On kids' TV shows, when someone's being a bad boy, sometimes they replace him with a stuffed animal as an emergency measure. {lit. "doll" but decided to go more specific}

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:38.930
He probably died after being cut with this accidentally while we were all jostling together.

00:08:38.930 --> 00:08:40.600
Huh, there's a name written on it.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:48.620
I'm sorry!

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:53.380
Feels good man.

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.880
I've found the man from the school board, but where is everyone?

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:02.390
Everyone's here, just like they should be.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:05.190
I'm home.

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:08.530
... And that's what happened at school today.

00:09:13.480 --> 00:09:15.320
It's nice and warm here under the floor.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:18.010
Is this what they mean by in-floor heating?

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:21.510
Boss, we've missed the deadline!

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:25.010
Damn you, Kumeta!

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.850
Teacher is marking our tests.

00:09:35.850 --> 00:09:36.990
This is the first time I've seen him do it.

00:09:37.250 --> 00:09:40.480
Everyone, I'm giving your tests back! Sit down!

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:47.300
This was right, but you marked it wrong!

00:09:47.300 --> 00:09:48.780
Right, but marked wrong...

00:09:49.430 --> 00:09:51.110
Frequently, for adults,

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:53.270
there are things for which the correct answer isn't right!

00:09:54.110 --> 00:09:54.410
If I'm made the butt of a joke, I feel like I've lost

00:10:00.380 --> 00:10:01.780
The quiz show!

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.680
What's this all of a sudden?

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:06.420
Our first contestants will be the celebrity team.

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:11.420
What proverb involving kappa means the same thing as “Even monkeys fall out of trees”?          \h

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:08.050
Question:

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:11.440
What proverb involving kappa means the same thing as “Even mon—

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:13.640
When they get washed away?

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:17.230
What!? Isn't that right?

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.060
As an answer, it's—

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:21.800
We can't have celebrities answering normally.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.070
Ham it up a little, will ya?

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:25.820
Hey, Producer, don't use him anymore.

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:28.560
It's the correct answer, but it's not right!

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:34.730
For our next contestants, we have the Businessman Team.

00:10:36.210 --> 00:10:39.620
This time, we have a special request from the President.

00:10:39.970 --> 00:10:41.950
Go ahead, sir.

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.970
Do you know who Da-bleep-go's grandfather is?

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:47.660
Former PM Takeshita?

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:49.550
Yeah...

00:10:49.550 --> 00:10:50.280
That's right...

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.980
Didn't even the President say it was right!?

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:54.960
It's correct.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.520
However, it's not right. In terms of fitting your lifestyle.

00:10:58.000 --> 00:10:59.000
You.

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:01.710
I'm sorry, I don't follow fads.

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:04.010
Is someone someone famous's grandson?

00:11:04.010 --> 00:11:05.050
Correct.

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:06.510
That's not even an answer!

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.630
{ma}What a trite program.

00:11:09.220 --> 00:11:10.760
Melancholy of Majiru.{MAJIRU NO YUUUTSU}

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:15.400
{ko}Majiru, what did you buy with your stimulus check?

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:16.770
I bought DVDs.

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:22.030
That'll make you feel better along with the economy.

00:11:22.390 --> 00:11:23.370
I bought these!

00:11:23.370 --> 00:11:26.870
Eh? These aren't anime DVDs.

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:29.370
Next, the Ministry of Defense Team.

00:11:29.780 --> 00:11:33.100
From here on, I'll be asking my class to participate, too.

00:11:33.560 --> 00:11:41.550
Which country's submarine violated our maritime borders around Kochi Prefecture's Cape Ashi-bleep-misaki and the Bungo Channel?

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.620
The sound of the propellers should give you a hint.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:46.120
{BIM-BOM}Buzz.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.580
You were there?

00:11:47.580 --> 00:11:48.490
Give me your answer.

00:11:48.490 --> 00:11:49.690
Chi—

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:56.030
Huh? Anyone who knows anything about submarine sounds agrees it has to be a Han-class nuclear sub!

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:56.030
That's correct, but it's not right.

00:11:56.030 --> 00:11:57.360
Tell me why.

00:11:57.360 --> 00:11:59.360
Let's hear it from the former Minister. {check later}

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:04.370
The correct answer is, “It was a submarine from an unknown country, or perhaps a whale mistaken for one.”

00:12:04.370 --> 00:12:06.340
That was a tough one.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:07.870
No, it's common sense.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:07.870
Next, a silhouette quiz.

00:12:08.180 --> 00:12:09.370
Who is this person?

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:15.380
Hint 1: Entered the country with a fake passport
Hint 2: Hung out at a certain theme park {fix for anim later}

00:12:15.650 --> 00:12:16.380
{tc}Buzz!

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:17.620
Jong—

00:12:17.620 --> 00:12:18.730
That's right, isn't it?

00:12:18.730 --> 00:12:20.560
That's correct, but in terms of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, it's not right.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:22.190
The correct answer is—

00:12:22.190 --> 00:12:24.500
That's not even an answer!

00:12:23.470 --> 00:12:26.660
Modern Japan has made that the answer!

00:12:26.660 --> 00:12:27.960
All right, next question.

00:12:27.960 --> 00:12:29.210
An artificial satellite.

00:12:29.860 --> 00:12:32.610
Too much cold medicine.

00:12:33.260 --> 00:12:38.890
If we have a tax on DVDs we can get money even from those who don't pay income tax.

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.540
Put season 4 on a major broadcaster, 5PM Sundays.

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:43.640
No way.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.890
Can you <i>not</i> be so down on that last one?

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:50.350
Irrationality where the correct answer isn't right.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:54.350
Saying “McDonal” like your English teacher taught you, but no one understands!

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:59.290
Driving  the right speed (the limit) means you tie up traffic and they honk!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:07.300
If a customer hyped up to travel asks “where is the ocean beautiful?”, when you answer “Okinawa” they'll feel let down!

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:10.800
This world where the correct answer isn't right has left me in despair!

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:10.680
Make Calpis with the proper dose and get called out for being cheap
Pay full price airfare, feel cheated
Made faces at after being asked how old someone looks
Ending in the friend zone
Look like you're showing off when asked how to pronounce Jaguar
Play the piece straight up and it doesn't tug at heartstrings
Be a proper adult and bring a lost girl to the police, get arrested
Talk about your beloved wife from Holland, attract weird looks
Tranny entering the toilet listed on their birth certificate, shocking people
Receipt from a strip club saying "** Tours" rather than the real name
Kept locked up, and found guilty, because you insisted you didn't do it
It seems there was a marvellous bureaucrat who, insisting that black-market rice was bad, died of starvation
In order to follow the constitution, get wiped out while waiting for orders to fire
Hit and runs under the current traffic law (including drugs)
Insist on proper separation of church and state, and who will come
Insist on basic human rights and give more to criminals than victims
Collecting welfare even though they could work
Panties-shaped glasses cleaner
Two men riding a bike "combining"
Buying LDs, buying DVDs, buying BDs...  How many of the same thing are you gonna buy?
Spoiler/notes sites
We talk about S4, but really, how about Kaizo or Southern...

00:13:11.120 --> 00:13:15.080
This is a pretty dull program. They should put anime on.

00:13:15.080 --> 00:13:15.910
Correct.

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.710
Next is the up-down quiz.

00:13:17.710 --> 00:13:20.730
Everyone, try to lift Teacher's gondola with your answers!

00:13:20.730 --> 00:13:22.430
What, I'm not asking?

00:13:23.080 --> 00:13:24.430
All right, question!

00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.420
Which one sells better, A or B?

00:13:26.420 --> 00:13:27.770
A!

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.420
Even though I was right, he's going down!

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:35.160
Yep, this is a "feelings up-down" quiz!

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:39.050
It seems like, even though it was the correct answer, it wasn't right.

00:13:39.050 --> 00:13:42.310
At that point, it was a downer.

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:44.900
{ke}If she's for real, now, I—!

00:13:44.900 --> 00:13:49.310
Everyone, try to answer without bringing the person in the gondola down!

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:52.840
{mx}I'm speaking from the loser's circle. Let's interview him.

00:13:52.840 --> 00:13:55.510
How does it feel to be a loser?

00:13:55.510 --> 00:13:57.590
I haven't lost!

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:59.290
This was an interview from the loser's circle.

00:13:59.290 --> 00:14:02.670
Next, let's take a question from her in the gondola.

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:03.290
Question!

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:06.290
People like me should just die, shouldn't they?

00:14:08.560 --> 00:14:10.010
No way!

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:12.670
Many people hold you dear!

00:14:12.670 --> 00:14:14.680
Don't give me that, you hypocrite!

00:14:15.260 --> 00:14:18.380
You only say that because you don't care about me!

00:14:18.380 --> 00:14:19.540
She's going down!

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:20.270
Then...

00:14:20.680 --> 00:14:22.740
If you wanna die, go ahead and do it.

00:14:21.970 --> 00:14:22.740
That's horrible!

00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:25.190
I'll really do it!

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:26.770
Either way, she goes down.

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:28.490
This quiz doesn't go anywhere but down, does it!?

00:14:28.490 --> 00:14:30.720
Going up has its own dangers.

00:14:31.060 --> 00:14:33.020
Next question after commercials!

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:34.220
Don't change that channel!

00:14:34.690 --> 00:14:37.240
{cm}Get Lasik, and you'll be popular with the girls!

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:38.070
Maybe I should get Lasik.

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:40.230
You're fine how you are, Majiru.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:44.230
All right, time for the next question.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.970
You're pretty far down, aren't you?

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:49.460
This is decisive proof!

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:50.840
With this, we can solve the mystery!

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.500
The murderer is the victim's five-year-old son!

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:54.840
That's correct, Zetsubou.

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:56.310
However...

00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:57.580
What are you doing!?

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.580
It's true, but it's not right.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:04.850
If a five-year-old killed his mother, his father would never stop beating him.

00:15:04.850 --> 00:15:07.890
Even if he were pardoned, society would make a racket about it.

00:15:07.890 --> 00:15:10.090
My response to that is to bring the investigation to a dead end.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:13.630
Chiri's sis attended this guy's funeral, right?

00:15:13.630 --> 00:15:15.600
He's the fourth out of six brothers.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.230
Cut!

00:15:17.590 --> 00:15:19.850
Teacher, this is no time to be playing around! {as in, uh, participating in a play, hurr}

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:21.340
Look over here!

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:23.640
A time tunnel is opening up!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:25.110
Let's go!

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:33.370
The heavens revolve around the Earth!

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:36.440
After all, God placed the Earth in the center of all.

00:15:36.440 --> 00:15:37.940
What are you talking about?

00:15:37.940 --> 00:15:40.690
Of course the Earth moves.

00:15:40.690 --> 00:15:42.160
Heretic!

00:15:44.190 --> 00:15:49.190
If you tell people the Earth moves in this era, even though it's correct, it's not the right answer.

00:15:49.190 --> 00:15:50.000
You were there?

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.700
Always.

00:15:51.700 --> 00:15:53.880
Teacher, a loophole!

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:55.670
This way, you can avoid being burned at the stake!

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:58.620
I've been saved!

00:15:58.620 --> 00:15:59.170
Teacher.

00:15:59.170 --> 00:16:01.690
What color clothing is the King wearing?

00:16:01.690 --> 00:16:02.690
The King's clothing?

00:16:10.680 --> 00:16:12.200
The King is naked.

00:16:16.190 --> 00:16:19.190
It's correct, but it wasn't the right answer.

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:25.010
Your highness, these are clothes that only Merumeru can see.

00:16:25.010 --> 00:16:26.470
Sold!

00:16:26.470 --> 00:16:28.970
Isn't this dress wonderful?

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:30.970
Koji! Koji!

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:32.990
He's just some random pervert, officer.

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.020
Incredible range!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:48.620
Nice shot!

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:55.230
Well, <i>amateurs</i> may be satisfied with range no matter what their score.

00:16:57.430 --> 00:17:03.020
However, in this world, there are times when it may not be best to have too much of a range.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:06.240
I came today to measure your range.

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:06.410
How much can I break labor laws

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:06.570
How far can I stretch the schedule

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:06.710
How short can I cut my sleep schedule

00:17:06.710 --> 00:17:06.910
How long can I put off paying my premiums

00:17:06.910 --> 00:17:07.040
How little can I pay for food

00:17:07.040 --> 00:17:07.340
How much longer can I keep up this line of work, I wonder

00:17:11.590 --> 00:17:14.230
I came today to measure your range.

00:17:14.820 --> 00:17:17.490
What are you talking about? Isn't that paradoxical?

00:17:17.490 --> 00:17:22.990
Brother, a new course has been completed! Bring everyone!

00:17:24.490 --> 00:17:26.340
This is just our town.

00:17:26.340 --> 00:17:30.600
I see, building a golf course in town. That's an easy plan.

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:32.350
Hole 1.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:38.280
This is the tee for the first hole.

00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:39.610
It's just someone's room!

00:17:39.610 --> 00:17:42.540
Let's see what this boy's range is.

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:45.260
By the way, this doesn't use balls or clubs.

00:17:52.180 --> 00:17:53.930
Ah, he left his room!

00:17:53.930 --> 00:17:55.090
Nice shot!

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:58.830
He put on a sweatsuit! Maybe he's going to the corner store.

00:18:03.960 --> 00:18:05.710
He got on a train! In a sweatsuit!

00:18:12.570 --> 00:18:15.180
In the end, he went to the theater with a friend!

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:18.380
That's quite the range!

00:18:18.440 --> 00:18:20.850
The range from home he can go while wearing a sweatsuit!

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:24.950
Speaking of which, this is how you keep score of that.

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:28.060
I can only make it down to the corner store!

00:18:28.560 --> 00:18:30.070
Hole 2.

00:18:32.260 --> 00:18:36.310
Hole 2. That man is the tee.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:38.330
Let's see his range.

00:18:39.310 --> 00:18:40.920
He parked in the middle of the road!

00:18:40.920 --> 00:18:41.570
Yes.

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:45.170
He's seeing how far away he can get from his car, having parked in the middle of the road downtown!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:48.400
No way! I can't make it out of sight!

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:49.950
Because they're cracking down.

00:18:50.250 --> 00:18:51.680
Hole 3.

00:18:51.680 --> 00:18:55.130
Hole 3. A theme park is the tee.

00:18:57.650 --> 00:18:58.850
Closing time.

00:19:08.530 --> 00:19:11.900
Just how far can he make it away from the park without taking those ears off!?

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:16.450
A girl or a child would be fine...

00:19:16.450 --> 00:19:18.290
But a grown man can't pull it off.

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:22.580
For this kind of thing, too long of a range becomes problematic.

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:25.210
Like how far an office lady can make it with no makeup!

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:28.820
Or how far a salaryman's single-family house in the suburbs is from his office!

00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:32.320
Or how far a parent can go while leaving their baby locked in the car!

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:36.330
And there's one especially difficult course I think all men want to try just once.

00:19:36.640 --> 00:19:38.330
Hole 4.

00:19:40.070 --> 00:19:42.300
How far they can make it naked!

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:44.300
That's just being a pervert!

00:19:44.760 --> 00:19:46.590
He's made it to the street in front of his apartment!

00:19:46.590 --> 00:19:47.840
Nice shot!

00:19:47.840 --> 00:19:49.640
He's flying, all the way down to the shopping plaza!

00:19:49.640 --> 00:19:51.290
Look at him go!

00:19:51.290 --> 00:19:53.910
You've got to call out so you don't hit the gallery!

00:19:56.320 --> 00:20:00.740
Fore!

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:01.620
People are avoiding him!

00:20:01.620 --> 00:20:03.040
Of course!

00:20:04.450 --> 00:20:06.120
I made it all the way to the station.

00:20:06.120 --> 00:20:07.190
Nice, par.

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.190
Hole 5.

00:20:11.790 --> 00:20:12.800
Meru?

00:20:13.180 --> 00:20:15.400
This is a tough course for girls nowadays.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:18.000
How far can you get without your cell phone!?

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.410
That's amazingly short.

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:26.720
She didn't even leave her room!

00:20:26.990 --> 00:20:30.210
For this, it's not having much range that's the problem.

00:20:32.150 --> 00:20:33.550
What's this?

00:20:33.550 --> 00:20:35.630
Brother, you're the tee.

00:20:40.920 --> 00:20:42.390
I can't make it any further!

00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:45.800
How far can a stalker make it from their target?

00:20:45.800 --> 00:20:48.610
Not having much range is a problem here, too!

00:20:52.780 --> 00:20:53.640
What?

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:57.110
How far will shut-ins go to buy Jump?

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:01.410
That's not very much range, even for a shut-in.

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:02.050
Give me a break!

00:21:02.340 --> 00:21:04.980
I can at least manage a birdie!

00:22:41.510 --> 00:22:44.790
The Zetsubou-sensei Drawing Song is about to start.

00:22:44.790 --> 00:22:47.840
Matching the song, let's draw leisurely, okay?

00:22:48.610 --> 00:22:54.980
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:22:54.980 --> 00:23:01.570
A tulip leans in the wind, and lays flat.

00:23:01.570 --> 00:23:02.990
Lightning...

00:23:02.990 --> 00:23:04.690
Flash!

00:23:04.690 --> 00:23:06.370
Lightning...

00:23:06.370 --> 00:23:07.990
Flash!

00:23:07.990 --> 00:23:11.140
The rain comes pouring down.

00:23:11.140 --> 00:23:14.400
From the gaps came the leaks.

00:23:14.400 --> 00:23:17.570
Two puddles were made.

00:23:17.570 --> 00:23:20.720
Let's go fishing, there's the fish hook!

00:23:20.720 --> 00:23:25.020
With the fish we caught, we made a fish cake.

00:23:25.300 --> 00:23:28.900
It's Zetsubou-sensei!

00:23:28.900 --> 00:23:31.540
Did everyone draw well?

00:23:31.540 --> 00:23:33.560
Bye bye!
